  "reason": "Existing evidence is sparse: RNA-only scvi_n200 singleprofile is the best result so far (0.520 accuracy, 0.498 F1), PCA RNA is weaker (0.485, 0.464), and image-only ResNet50 is weak (0.208, 0.172). The key uncertainty is whether another RNA representation, scgpt, can improve over the current best RNA encoder. config_007 tests scgpt under the same singleprofile RNA-only setting, isolating the representation choice without adding profile, aggregation, or fusion complexity. This is the best next use of budget because it directly reduces uncertainty about an important design decision and identifies the strongest RNA baseline before testing more complex multiprofile or multimodal configurations."
